Falsifies `address_space_layout::verification::window_accepts_every_whole_window_its_band_holds`.

The defect: `window` asks the band to hold one page more than the window, so a window that ends at the band's end is refused.

Expected to fail: Kani reports "a window must lie wholly inside its band" reachable for a window ending at `RUNTIME_WINDOWS.end`.

diff --git a/crates/address_space_layout/src/lib.rs b/crates/address_space_layout/src/lib.rs
index cb71c3977..d58d9d550 100644
--- a/crates/address_space_layout/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/address_space_layout/src/lib.rs
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ pub const fn window(band: Band, start_virtual_address: u64, bytes: u64) -> u64 {
         panic!("a window must not wrap past the top of the address space");
     };
     assert!(
-        band.holds(start_virtual_address, end_virtual_address),
+        band.holds(start_virtual_address, end_virtual_address + PAGE),
         "a window must lie wholly inside its band"
     );
     start_virtual_address
